<given-names>HN</given-names></name><name><surname>Hammond</surname><given-names>GD</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Early response to induction therapy as a predictor of disease-free survival and late recurrence of childhood acute lymphoblastic leukemia: a report from the Children's Cancer Study Group</article-title><source>J Clin Oncol</source><year>1989</year><volume>7</volume><fpage>1807</fpage><lpage>1815</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2685179</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kitchingman</surname><given-names>GR</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Residual disease detection in multiple follow-up samples in children with acute lymphoblastic leukemia</article-title><source>Leukemia</source><year>1994</year><volume>8</volume><fpage>395</fpage><lpage>401</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8127144</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Biondi</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Yokota</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Hansen-Hagge</surname><given-names>TE</given-names></name><name><surname>Rossi</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Giudici</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Maglia</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name><name><surname>Basso</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Tell</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Masera</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Bartram</surname><given-names>CR</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Minimal residual disease in childhood acute lymphoblastic leukemia: analysis of patients in continuous complete remission or with consecutive relapse</article-title><source>Leukemia</source><year>1992</year><volume>6</volume><fpage>282</fpage><lpage>28